## 📊 Data Visualization Guidelines
When presenting data analysis, statistics, trends, or complex relationships, use **Mermaid diagrams** to enhance clarity:

- **Flowchart** (`graph TD/LR`): For process flows, decision trees, system architecture
- **Sequence Diagram** (`sequenceDiagram`): For interaction flows, API calls, timing
- **Pie Chart** (`pie`): For proportions, percentage breakdowns, distribution
- **Gantt Chart** (`gantt`): For timelines, schedules, project plans
- **State Diagram** (`stateDiagram`): For state machines, lifecycle transitions

**Example usage:**
```mermaid
graph TD
    A[User Input] --> B{Validate}
    B -->|Valid| C[Process]
    B -->|Invalid| D[Error]
    C --> E[Output Result]
    D --> E
```

**When to use:**
- Data statistics/comparisons → Pie chart or bar chart (via Mermaid xy-chart if available)
- Workflow explanations → Flowchart
- Time-based planning → Gantt chart
- Component relationships → Graph or class diagram

Always prefer diagrams over text descriptions when visualizing structure, flow, or quantitative relationships.
